unibench's forkserver_libafl fuzzer, forkserver -> in-process, without AutoTokens.

Applies after unibench's own patches (forkserver_libafl_baseline,
forkserver_toml_monitor, forkserver_libafl_dryrun, forkserver_libafl_sigint,
copied verbatim from Reusing-unibench_build/forkserver_libafl/) and after
fuzzers/forkserver_libafl_cc/src/main.rs -- the fuzzer unibench runs -- is
copied over fuzzers/fuzzbench/src/lib.rs (see builder.Dockerfile). The diff to
src/lib.rs is therefore the complete difference from that fuzzer:

  - executor   ForkserverExecutor -> InProcessExecutor over the target's
               LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput, after LLVMFuzzerInitialize
  - observer   the edges map in __AFL_SHM_ID shared memory -> the same map
               in this process (std_edges_map_observer, same name)
  - tokens     the tokens the forkserver target sends -> autotokens() from
               this binary (empty here, see below)
  - restarts   SimpleEventManager -> SimpleRestartingEventManager: a crash
               kills this process, so a fresh one resumes from the state left
               in shared memory
  - output     the target's stdout/stderr go to /dev/null, as the forkserver
               child's did; the monitor writes to a copy of stdout
  - CLI        no target executable, target arguments, --debug-child or
               --signal; libafl_main() is the entry the target's main calls

Cargo.toml and src/bin/libafl_cc.rs take unibench's instrumentation and the
unibench crate's dependencies: trace-pc-guard only (no trace-cmp, no
CmpLogRtn pass, no sancov_cmplog runtime), clap with derive, env_logger.

One deliberate difference from unibench: no AutoTokens pass. The target then
has no libafl_token section, autotokens() returns no tokens, and the tokens
mutations find nothing to insert -- a run without any dictionary. (unibench's
forkserver_libafl_baseline.patch adds the pass to forkserver_libafl_cc.)

